Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["CG Coefficients", "Title",
 CellID->529115844,ExpressionUUID->"36a8a731-d81c-461f-b9ca-d31dc0b24bed"],

Cell["\<\
Matchete includes a framework for dealing with contractions of Clebsch-Gordan \
coefficients (CGs) in a pseudo-symbolic manner. The workflow involves \
associating explicit tensor representations to each symbolic CG. This allows \
contractions to be evaluated numerically (exact) with tensor contractions \
before the result is projected onto a basis consisting of the already defined \
CGs.     \
\>", "Text",
 CellID->120207881,ExpressionUUID->"2e21bd4d-6283-4f1e-a7f2-e82d3ea99592"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Setting up CGs", "Section",
 CellID->1239290677,ExpressionUUID->"61419a22-d63b-4ec7-9795-e89aef97bb9b"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Organizing the symbolic CGs", "Subsection",
 CellID->1598132758,ExpressionUUID->"2324f8e4-9a2e-4f3f-8802-6cff733e48de"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "All CGs transform under the action of a particular (gauge) group. It would \
be absurd to start talking about contracting invariants of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"SU", "(", "2", ")"}], "L"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "81344a39-8373-4210-b539-8506db12307f"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"SU", "(", "3", ")"}], "c"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "91e48366-25f8-47d6-8948-bd91b57c6faa"],
 ". Even contractions between two distinct SU(2) groups would not be \
sensible. To allow for evaluations in scenarios with multiple group indices, \
as required in realistic QFTs such as the SM, we must first define the \
symmetry groups and the relevant representations. "
}], "Text",
 CellID->751867057,ExpressionUUID->"54818093-567e-4c66-b557-6cb9aca06a63"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      ButtonBox["DefineCGGroup",
       BaseStyle->"Link",
       ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/DefineCGGroup"], "[", 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["groupName", "TI"], ",", " ", 
       StyleBox["alg", "TI"]}], "]"}], " "}], Cell[
    "initializaes a Lie group with a reference name and algebra. ", 
     "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"5b611532-63e3-4c8b-9526-c882ff5ae7bf"]},
   {
    RowBox[{
     ButtonBox["DefineRepresentation",
      BaseStyle->"Link",
      ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/DefineRepresentation"], "[", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["repName", "TI"], ",", " ", 
      StyleBox["groupName", "TI"], ",", " ", 
      StyleBox["rep", "TI"]}], "]"}], Cell["\<\
initializes a representation under a group with a representation name and its \
Dynkin coefficients.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"a82f97b3-80ca-46cb-9620-12ed8e62c383"]}
  }]], "DefinitionBox",
 CellID->121675449,ExpressionUUID->"2c79d0ad-20d9-4b63-bb7b-258c2a910d2e"],

Cell["\<\
Routines to initializes Lie groups and their representations.\
\>", "Caption",
 CellID->594839399,ExpressionUUID->"59ff6ea8-48f6-4cd0-a12d-f9ab473cdc01"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A group is initialized by giving it a reference name and specifying its Lie \
algebra (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Alg",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/Alg"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "50561449-3589-4b13-8f91-8a8ff024b033"],
 "), which informs all the representation theory associated with said group. \
The group name is a label that the user should use to refer to that specific \
group. The use of group names ensures that multiple groups with identical \
algebra can be discriminated. The user may, thus, define multiple SU(2) \
groups in the same session. When a group has been defined, one can define \
representations of that group to be used in Lagrangians of group theory \
contractions. "
}], "Text",
 CellID->1193843836,ExpressionUUID->"53d29ce3-8a46-41fe-bb4a-a6b2c42b65b9"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "We may define a group, by specifying an arbitrary group label (",
 StyleBox["SU3c", "Input"],
 "),  and an algebra (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["SU",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/SU"], "[", "3", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"7bcd5464-bf7a-43cd-b136-bf8aef32e13b"],
 " in this case).  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["GetGroups",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/GetGroups"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"0c1d41c1-63b1-49db-9cfe-1c1b9a65fbba"],
 " can be used to get an association with all the groups that have been \
defined in the current session."
}], "MathCaption",
 CellID->303616520,ExpressionUUID->"80f42a23-ed51-4c9f-95ca-8eb57130fa3b"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"DefineCGGroup", "[", 
  RowBox[{"SU3c", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"SU", "[", "3", "]"}]}], "]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"GetGroups", "[", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:=",
 CellID->461706368,ExpressionUUID->"380e4cf4-20ff-43ca-bfe2-cc98987c2ff4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
  RowBox[{"SU3c", "\[Rule]", 
   RowBox[{"Alg", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"A\"\>", ",", "2"}], "]"}]}], 
  "\[RightAssociation]"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[3]=",
 CellID->797849066,ExpressionUUID->"413b966f-9810-42a4-a33e-43c0f1af14eb"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "We can then add representations for our SU(3) group that we wish to use in \
calculations. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["DefineRepresentations",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/DefineRepresentations"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"78d61887-c5bd-4cf2-91a2-fd273b928a97"],
 " takes an arbitrary label used to reference it, the name of the group it \
belongs to, and the Dynkin coefficients specifying the (highest weight of \
the) representation in the group algebra. Here we define a fundamental, a \
2-index symmetric, and an adjoint representations of our SU(3) group, while \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["GetRepresentations",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/GetRepresentations"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"61e11d1f-f302-4bfc-9dae-258698cf936f"],
 " returns an association with details about all representations defined in \
the current session:   "
}], "MathCaption",
 CellID->1390555871,ExpressionUUID->"f4a0a967-1a31-4782-93f3-9260ced57d0f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"DefineRepresentation", "[", 
  RowBox[{"fund", ",", " ", "SU3c", ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "0"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"DefineRepresentation", "[", 
  RowBox[{"S2", ",", " ", "SU3c", ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", "0"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"DefineRepresentation", "[", 
   RowBox[{"adj", ",", " ", "SU3c", ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " "}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"GetRepresentations", "[", "adj", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:=",
 CellID->7993596,ExpressionUUID->"862c3b1c-047d-4157-b4ec-e5114583e299"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Group", "\[Rule]", "SU3c"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"DynkinCoefficients", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"Dimension", "\[Rule]", "8"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"Reality", "\[Rule]", "\<\"Real\"\>"}]}], 
  "\[RightAssociation]"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[7]=",
 CellID->561360394,ExpressionUUID->"e8dbd594-7938-40fa-981b-1db488927c37"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["N.b.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["DefineCGGroup",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/DefineCGGroup"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"84506ef6-4dc8-4575-b282-b81d64505c04"],
 " is too bare bones for QFT applications. The user is encouraged to use ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["DefineGaugeGroup",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/DefineGaugeGroup"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"a7e94b78-9bd3-4925-9f45-719b77cf0c43"],
 " or ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["DefineGlobalGroup",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/DefineGlobalGroup"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"78817ab0-3526-491d-a351-be2057b03786"],
 " instead according to circumstances. These functions specifies important \
additional information about the QFT to ",
 ButtonBox["Matchete",
  BaseStyle->"Link",
  ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/guide/Matchete"],
 " in addition to automatically setting up some common representations and \
and CGs. "
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{8, 2}, {2, 2}},
 CellFrameMargins->{{16, 8}, {8, 8}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0, 0.3168, 0.5928],
 CellFrameStyle->{},
 CellFrameLabelMargins->6,
 Background->RGBColor[0.9, 0.9316800000000001, 0.95928],
 CellID->1581854326,ExpressionUUID->"7af6f9a2-22e1-4384-ba59-bd465edb44c8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Indices in Matchete \[LongDash] for fields, CGs, derivatives, etc. \
\[LongDash] all have an index type. They are represented internally with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["Index",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/Index"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["label", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["type", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "fc35a92d-27be-4f11-bbff-582b06c3b598"],
 ", and all the representations that have been defined are valid index types. \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Bar",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/Bar"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "27ed9a4a-8478-4cf4-9d6a-bfd7d0137ab7"],
 " is used to denote conjugate indices for indices in pseudoreal or complex \
representations. Complex and pseudoreal representations are always supposed \
to contract between conjugate indices with the same label. "
}], "Text",
 CellID->1274985093,ExpressionUUID->"eac5eada-2689-472c-b05d-439390226f4d"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Indices with label ",
 StyleBox["'a'",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " of the SU(3) fundamental representation we defined here are  (for the \
ordinary index and its conjugate) "
}], "MathCaption",
 CellID->982528278,ExpressionUUID->"5cf91441-ac82-4b48-88ce-383c2a4f14c4"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Index", "[", 
   RowBox[{"a", ",", "fund"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Bar", "@", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Index", "[", 
    RowBox[{"a", ",", "fund"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:=",
 CellID->1351006563,ExpressionUUID->"929552f9-2c67-4d04-854b-41c09bfb2311"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Defining CGs", "Subsection",
 CellID->1893821422,ExpressionUUID->"283b4670-6231-4a63-af5c-5acc987e8daf"],

Cell["\<\
Having defined groups and representations it becomes possible to define new \
CGs for use in calculations. Matchete needs information about the \
representation of all indices on the CG symbol and should have an exact \
numerical tensor to substitute in for the symbol when performing contractions \
with other CGs. Currently, there are two ways for the user to specify a new \
CG symbol to the program.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1839337075,ExpressionUUID->"7b8599a6-25e3-4384-9afe-399163c086bf"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {
    RowBox[{
     ButtonBox["DefineCG",
      BaseStyle->"Link",
      ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/DefineCG"], "[", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["cgName", "TI"], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["rep", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["1", "TR"]], ",", " ", 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["rep", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["2", "TR"]], ",", " ", "\[Ellipsis]"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      StyleBox["tensor", "TI"]}], "]"}], Cell["\<\
defines a CG symbol with indices in the the representations from a numerical \
tensor. \
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"6f53499c-3325-4d7b-b427-c0281cac5e7f"]},
   {
    RowBox[{
     ButtonBox["DefineCompositeCG",
      BaseStyle->"Link",
      ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/DefineCompositeCG"], "[", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["cgName", "TI"], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["cg", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["1", "TR"]], ",", " ", 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["cg", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["2", "TR"]], ",", "\[Ellipsis]"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["indices", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["1", "TR"]], ",", " ", 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["indices", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["2", "TR"]], ",", "\[Ellipsis]"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], 
    Cell["\<\
defines a CG symbol as a contraction (Einstein summation) of known CGs.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"74b05ac4-b5ff-4439-abd9-aefc1a4e0137"]}
  }]], "DefinitionBox",
 CellID->1728747875,ExpressionUUID->"86fd653c-56cd-46c5-b649-d696cf021db9"],

Cell["Routines for defining new CG symbols in a session.", "Caption",
 CellID->1759274862,ExpressionUUID->"6de890b1-af30-4ef4-8cbb-9b435b7e4faa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The most direct way of defining a CG is to use ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["DefineCG",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/DefineCG"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"d6fe0afd-5e8b-4490-b55c-d54b96596454"],
 ". It requires 3 arguments: a label, a list of the representations of the \
indices, and an explicit sparse array with the numerical values for the \
tensor. Typically, the functions made available for the group invariants are \
used to construct/find explicit invariant tensors as detailed in ",
 ButtonBox["Group Magic",
  BaseStyle->"Link",
  ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/tutorial/GroupMagic"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1615462772,ExpressionUUID->"1de036c7-a5b7-46f5-b1df-0af0a6ed43d2"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Returning to the example of the adjoint representation ",
 StyleBox["adj",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " for our SU(3) group ",
 StyleBox["SU3c",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ",",
 StyleBox[" ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 "we may define various CG coefficient corresponding to different invariant \
contractions of those indices. Here we define a Kronecker delta, the \
structure constants and the three-index symmetric invariant: "
}], "MathCaption",
 CellID->1403574612,ExpressionUUID->"0c8b6678-e0ed-4bd2-a2fb-3c52889f4367"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"DefineCG", "[", 
  RowBox[{"f3", ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"adj", ",", "adj", ",", "adj"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"StructureConstants", "@", 
    RowBox[{"SU", "[", "3", "]"}]}]}], "]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"DefineCG", "[", 
  RowBox[{"d3", ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"adj", ",", "adj", ",", "adj"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"First", "@", 
    RowBox[{"InvariantTensors", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"SU", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", "1"}], "}"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", "1"}], "}"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"SymmetricIndices", "\[Rule]", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", "2", ",", "3"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Normalization", "\[Rule]", 
       RowBox[{"40", "/", "3"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], " ", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[10]:=",
 CellID->1918125236,ExpressionUUID->"efb5431e-d015-4a58-9463-e5a78ceaa104"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Here we have used ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["InvariantTensors",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/InvariantTensors"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"53648e88-1f2e-4a13-9980-98eddb739f46"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["StructureConstants",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/StructureConstants"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"45ad3a9b-617f-46f2-9c78-ab49066dff5b"],
 " to obtain the appropriate numerical tensor for each CG.  A Kronecker delta \
CG for the adjoint representation, named ",
 StyleBox["del[adj]",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", was automatically initialized when we defined the representation. At any \
time we can check the numerical tensor associated with a CG with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["GetCGTensor",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/GetCGTensor"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"d6061f42-ab46-4efe-b548-af8f7602ee60"],
 ":"
}], "MathCaption",
 CellID->1472525733,ExpressionUUID->"6d8f5e27-919f-4c41-9f7e-7164bcd7cdba"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"TensorRank", "@", 
  RowBox[{"GetCGTensor", "@", "f3"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"GetCGTensor", "@", 
  RowBox[{"del", "[", "adj", "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[12]:=",
 CellID->1628922480,ExpressionUUID->"ded58649-6126-4951-8ab5-d4d9be8a77b1"],

Cell[BoxData["3"], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[12]=",
 CellID->888480687,ExpressionUUID->"da64cbf7-6a9d-46c7-a39d-32137971edd8"],

