Cell[TextData[{
 "For indices of non-real representations, we need to distinguish between the \
indices and the conjugates. For instance, the Kronecker delta ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", "i"], "j"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "99dee97b-2cae-4c08-bcd8-94be85ae622d"],
 " associated with ",
 StyleBox["fund",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "  comes with a fundamental and an anti-fundamental index of SU(3). It \
contracts (is an invariant of) an anti-fundamental and a fundamental \
representations: the order is reversed. We may specify that an index of a CG \
belongs to the conjugate representation by applying a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Bar",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/Bar"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "aed611f8-559b-4f8c-a47a-df1c9dad813a"],
 " to the representation name. "
}], "Text",
 CellID->1563912461,ExpressionUUID->"b88ad71b-2924-4391-b674-d45ffde7de6f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Kronecker delta of the ",
 StyleBox["fund",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " representation of ",
 StyleBox["SU3c",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " is automatically defined with the representation and is named ",
 StyleBox["del[fund]",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". If the user wanted to define such a delta themself, it might look like "
}], "MathCaption",
 CellID->662124805,ExpressionUUID->"476376dc-5b87-4268-a142-6b66e043ad5b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"DefineCG", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\[Delta]fund", ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"fund", ",", 
     RowBox[{"Bar", "[", "fund", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"First", "@", 
    RowBox[{"InvariantTensors", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"SU", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"CRep", "[", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"1", ",", "0"}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[14]:=",
 CellID->71338881,ExpressionUUID->"8c487f90-76fc-40b2-ad84-9d5d4d6116b9"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "The first index is fundamental and the second anti-fundamental. Valid \
contractions should always contract fundamental and anti-fundamental indices \
to ensure proper covariance, since the representation is complex. Also the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["InvariantTensors",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/InvariantTensors"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"fbc440ee-d854-4b7d-9ce5-6f71e69d8bfa"],
 " call needs to discriminate between the two indices by invoking the \
conjugate representation with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["CRep",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/CRep"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "8a051705-691d-4623-9530-6fd2b33078a3"],
 ". Similarly, the generators of the fundamental representation comes with a \
fundamental and an anti-fundamental index. It can be initializes as "
}], "MathCaption",
 CellID->2030367325,ExpressionUUID->"77242d69-bd9c-4c9f-8137-29b270c33c63"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"DefineCG", "[", 
  RowBox[{"t3", ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"adj", ",", "fund", ",", 
     RowBox[{"Bar", "@", "fund"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"Generators", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SU", "@", "3"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", "0"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[15]:=",
 CellID->868480445,ExpressionUUID->"191a8300-3c52-4636-92bd-c6fff5daeacd"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["N.b.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "  The user has a lot of flexibility when defining new CGs, but it requires \
meticulous care to get it right. We encourage the user to perform crosschecks \
wherever possible, to ensure that their CGs behave as expected."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{8, 2}, {2, 2}},
 CellFrameMargins->{{16, 8}, {8, 8}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0, 0.3168, 0.5928],
 CellFrameStyle->{},
 CellFrameLabelMargins->6,
 Background->RGBColor[0.9, 0.9316800000000001, 0.95928],
 CellID->1168667819,ExpressionUUID->"579501a3-fcaf-4ff6-9b58-0fccbc497053"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Clearly, many other invariants can be constructed, but ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["DefineCG",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/DefineCG"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"cc986d86-eb7e-45d4-a963-dccbd33b0135"],
 " will already be sufficient for most purposes. Sometimes it can be useful \
to construct new CGs from contractions of previously defined CGs, rather than \
use the rather less transparent ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["InvariantTensors",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/InvariantTensors"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"de5a48cf-aa70-4590-9bd7-2a9d921e6b99"],
 " function to obtain a suitable numeric tensor. In such cases we can use the \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["DefineCompositeCG",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/DefineCompositeCG"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"a20ffd00-1ba1-48db-87a8-0b107058fa8c"],
 "  to initialize the CG. The first argument is the CG label; the second \
argument is a list of CGs to be included in this tensor; and the third and \
last argument is a list of list of index labels for each of the CGs, with \
repeated indices being contracted and the rest open. "
}], "Text",
 CellID->1447681770,ExpressionUUID->"733359a1-f45c-4e9b-95b5-24c5a5a4f34f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "For instance, there are 8 invariants of 4 adjoint SU(3) representations if \
there are no restrictions from tensor symmetries. A good basis CG could be \
taken as the trace of fundamental generators ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["T", 
     RowBox[{"a", " ", "b", " ", "c", " ", "d"}]], "=", 
    RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["t", "a"], " ", 
      SuperscriptBox["t", "b"], " ", 
      SuperscriptBox["t", "c"], " ", 
      SuperscriptBox["t", "d"]}], "]"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "9caf20cf-071a-4800-adad-a8d4b433e7e8"],
 ", which has 6 unique permutations of indices making up 6 linearly \
independent invariants. We define this CG with   "
}], "MathCaption",
 CellID->1692376651,ExpressionUUID->"d2e313dc-8fd3-4f55-b852-d1333b86183d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"DefineCompositeCG", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Tr4", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"t3", ",", "t3", ",", "t3", ",", "t3"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"a", ",", "i", ",", "j"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"b", ",", " ", "j", ",", " ", "k"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"c", ",", " ", "k", ",", "l"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"d", ",", " ", "l", ",", " ", "i"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[16]:=",
 CellID->353468842,ExpressionUUID->"996459ff-364d-405b-821c-4d8b892806e7"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The above input corresponds to the assignment ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["Tr4", 
     RowBox[{"a", " ", "b", " ", "c", " ", "d"}]], "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      SuperscriptBox["t3", 
       RowBox[{"a", " ", "i"}]], "j"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      SuperscriptBox["t3", 
       RowBox[{"b", " ", "j"}]], "k"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      SuperscriptBox["t3", 
       RowBox[{"c", " ", "k"}]], "l"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      SuperscriptBox["t3", 
       RowBox[{"d", " ", "l"}]], "i"]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "e65f06e7-40e1-4815-8860-4be49cb453c9"],
 ". "
}], "MathCaption",
 CellID->1341583228,ExpressionUUID->"957a2563-d0d1-4c67-978a-8b9ab4a86ac4"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The CG object", "Subsection",
 CellID->2121769318,ExpressionUUID->"c4584013-f2ae-472e-a14b-4998a43ac984"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      ButtonBox["CG",
       BaseStyle->"Link",
       ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/CG"], "[", 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["cgName", "TI"], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["index", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["1", "TR"]], ",", " ", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["index", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["2", "TR"]], ",", "\[Ellipsis]"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " "}], 
    Cell["represents a CG with two or more indices.", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"849c1dcf-4816-4a0d-88e2-4834b1a2ec21"]}
  }]], "DefinitionBox",
 CellID->868302416,ExpressionUUID->"dba98ba7-a027-49c1-b72a-cd2566ec5c1e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 ButtonBox["Matchete",
  BaseStyle->"Link",
  ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/guide/Matchete"],
 "  form of the CG object. "
}], "Caption",
 CellID->1407324347,ExpressionUUID->"b82cc08f-4022-4806-8d5e-28d5cf1be86f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The basic object in computations involving CGs is the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["CG",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/CG"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "d6a41343-b6e9-447b-bf58-2913cb5bda67"],
 " head. The first argument of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["CG",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/CG"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "c95a41d9-ae90-474d-8a12-baa610d39410"],
 " specifies the specific tensor (its label); the second argument is a list \
of its indices. For convenience we can enter a CG by specifying only the \
labels of the indices rather than entering them as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Index",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/Index"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "2bc55334-944a-4243-943a-a6c9e117865e"],
 " objects. The full indices are automatically constructed based on the CG \
object. One can only enter CG objects that have already been initialized in \
the current session. Thus, Matchete never encounters unknown CGs. The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["CG",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/CG"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "c8405323-1031-4e82-b067-af60590e84e0"],
 " objects are conveniently formatted under ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["NiceForm",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/NiceForm"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"0a503e91-7780-4efc-bd27-be5148ff7ced"],
 ", so that the user doesn't have to see the internal representation."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1474741865,ExpressionUUID->"0a586b0a-5d5d-4038-8ea0-be88a1ae3442"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "The generator of the ",
 StyleBox["fund",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " representation of ",
 StyleBox["SU3c",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " can be entered as"
}], "MathCaption",
 CellID->1727372414,ExpressionUUID->"580fa12b-01da-4b14-9bfe-7d5a71133251"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"CG", "[", 
  RowBox[{"t3", ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"a", ",", "i", ",", "j"}], "}"}]}], 
  "]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"%", "//", "NiceForm"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[23]:=",
 CellID->116738305,ExpressionUUID->"eb33b2c3-38a6-4046-a669-289240e008c2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"CG", "[", 
  RowBox[{"t3", ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Index", "[", 
      RowBox[{"a", ",", "adj"}], "]"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"Index", "[", 
      RowBox[{"i", ",", "fund"}], "]"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"Bar", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Index", "[", 
       RowBox[{"j", ",", "fund"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[23]=",
 CellID->686176941,ExpressionUUID->"5488cd72-8757-47e7-b6c7-6639ed953e43"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  StyleBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["t3", 
    StyleBox["j",
     FontSize->10], 
    StyleBox[
     TemplateBox[{"a", "i"},
      "RowDefault"],
     FontSize->10]], "StandardForm"], Matchete`NiceForm]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[24]//NiceForm=",
 CellID->588662997,ExpressionUUID->"ef8f1eb0-4a75-4bdd-bb58-f89f40b0dc96"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
A second even more ergonomic shorthand notation is created when the CG is \
defined. We may simply use the CG label as a function like\
\>", "MathCaption",
 CellID->411202049,ExpressionUUID->"361a656d-2b5a-4a83-b675-d65d0d8891f6"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"t3", "[", 
  RowBox[{"a", ",", "i", ",", "j"}], "]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"%", "//", "NiceForm"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[25]:=",
 CellID->470461497,ExpressionUUID->"2a89957f-1561-4f36-a89e-62f7b547bb06"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"CG", "[", 
  RowBox[{"t3", ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Index", "[", 
      RowBox[{"a", ",", "adj"}], "]"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"Index", "[", 
      RowBox[{"i", ",", "fund"}], "]"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"Bar", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Index", "[", 
       RowBox[{"j", ",", "fund"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[25]=",
 CellID->1100540010,ExpressionUUID->"93fe6d3d-fc27-4e7e-b7b6-e5b73430a62f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  StyleBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["t3", 
    StyleBox["j",
     FontSize->10], 
    StyleBox[
     TemplateBox[{"a", "i"},
      "RowDefault"],
     FontSize->10]], "StandardForm"], Matchete`NiceForm]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[26]//NiceForm=",
 CellID->499296459,ExpressionUUID->"d394e62c-da51-4d38-8928-9428d2295793"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Other than constructing the indices, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["CG",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/CG"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "43d9d2b0-3c76-4b9a-afb4-ad988a8913a7"],
 " does not do any evaluation: there is nothing to evaluate. Rather it is \
just the internal representation of a CG tensor. Sometimes one might wish to \
use the complex conjugate CG. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Bar",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/Bar"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "61fd226d-feb2-44a0-834a-7f232ccb195e"],
 " can be applied to CGs to get the complex conjugate.  "
}], "Text",
 CellID->1464852780,ExpressionUUID->"070e7aa2-59a8-428a-8e78-45e425267732"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Since the the fundamental generators are Hermitian, we observe that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Bar",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/Bar"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "b900f8c1-e948-4aff-91a6-a27b24151e67"],
 " simplifies away: "
}], "MathCaption",
 CellID->1915966080,ExpressionUUID->"93423e07-815c-46a0-b748-b467b4fd0a5e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"Bar", "@", 
  RowBox[{"t3", "[", 
   RowBox[{"a", ",", "i", ",", "j"}], "]"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"%", "//", "NiceForm"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[27]:=",
 CellID->124619795,ExpressionUUID->"f8455a3c-42b3-484f-b2d0-a92a87075fda"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"CG", "[", 
  RowBox[{"t3", ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Index", "[", 
      RowBox[{"a", ",", "adj"}], "]"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"Index", "[", 
      RowBox[{"j", ",", "fund"}], "]"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"Bar", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Index", "[", 
       RowBox[{"i", ",", "fund"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[27]=",
 CellID->1661152040,ExpressionUUID->"78b2cf90-0420-4b47-88d7-720ffe4af301"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  StyleBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["t3", 
    StyleBox["i",
     FontSize->10], 
    StyleBox[
     TemplateBox[{"a", "j"},
      "RowDefault"],
     FontSize->10]], "StandardForm"], Matchete`NiceForm]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[28]//NiceForm=",
 CellID->1694925280,ExpressionUUID->"5b48cce4-569a-463e-8534-27201952620e"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["N.b.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "  When applying ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Bar",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/Bar"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "d4c8cf4b-4e43-4df2-826c-f376d3c51a98"],
 " to a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["CG",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Matchete/ref/CG"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "f91b6000-db0f-4c90-a391-d89fd7feb192"],
 " it turns the indices of any non-real representation into indices of the \
conjugate representation and vice versa."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{8, 2}, {2, 2}},
 CellFrameMargins->{{16, 8}, {8, 8}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0, 0.3168, 0.5928],
 CellFrameStyle->{},
